# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ABox: Workflow composition example (STARTER — extend this!)
#
# This example shows a Workflow with only ONE step. A single-step Workflow
# is technically valid but not very useful — the whole point of Workflows
# is to compose multiple actions into a workflow. Extend this by:
#
#   1. Adding at least one more step using p-plan:isStepOfPlan
#   2. Defining the execution order with p-plan:isPrecededBy
#   3. (Optional) Making the Workflow composable by giving it input/output
#      schemas, so it can itself be used as a step in higher-level Workflows
#
# IMPORTANT: Because your Thing Descriptions live in separate containers
# on your Pod, you must use FULL URIs to reference actions here — not
# bare fragment identifiers. For example:
#   <https://wiser-solid-xi.interactions.ics.unisg.ch/YOUR-POD/tools/web-fetcher#fetchWebPage>
# instead of just <#fetchWebPage>.
#
# UPLOAD INSTRUCTIONS:
# Upload this to your Solid Pod using the Write panel, e.g.:
#   https://wiser-solid-xi.interactions.ics.unisg.ch/YOUR-POD/workflows/myWorkflow
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@prefix td:          <https://www.w3.org/2019/wot/td#> .
@prefix jsonschema:  <https://www.w3.org/2019/wot/json-schema#> .
@prefix p-plan:      <http://purl.org/net/p-plan#> .

# ─── A single-step "Workflow" ───────────────────────────────────
# NOTE: A one-step Workflow is just an action wrapped in a plan —
# it adds no value. Your task is to make this meaningful by
# composing at least two actions from different tools.

<https://wiser-solid-xi.interactions.ics.unisg.ch/YOUR-POD/tools/web-fetcher#fetchWebPage> p-plan:isStepOfPlan <#it> .

# TODO: Add more steps!